versions.analysis_for_next:
Version 3 is the best so far at 62.8 macro-F1. Neutral recall rose to 45 of 143, but 60 neutral texts still go to positive.

Those neutral texts labelled positive are mostly of five kinds:
- political and institutional events (EU debate, parliament session, an MP meeting citizens, an association's proposals, EU measures);
- product listings or specs with no praise (Dynaudio SUB, beer, art piece);
- horoscopes, religious quotes and Bible readings;
- practical help or instruction replies in chat;
- course or application notices.

Positive-gold shares are mostly culture, entertainment, celebrity, sport, tech or business-success content, or articles framed as interesting reads. So I will add an explicit neutral bucket: political or institutional events and debates, religious or horoscope texts, bare product names or specs, and practical how-to replies.

The negative texts labelled neutral (25) are mostly self-mocking reports of the poster's own small mishaps (eye bags, torn sneakers, effort removing nail polish) and moralising remarks. I will add the poster's own mishaps, even when joking, to negative.

I keep the rest of version 3 unchanged and stay under 400 words.
